Context
  Decision was that skill scripts belong under the skill and meta scripts under
  scripts/. That matches the documentation and the corpus: 0 of 39 official
  plugins have a top-level bin/, 3 use plugin-level scripts/, 6 use skill-level
  scripts/.

Considerations
  - Duplication was chosen deliberately over a shared directory. guile-repl-
    paths.sh is carried by all three skills and guile-repl-proxy.scm by two,
    because gh skill install copies one skill's subtree and a skill that reaches
    outside it works from a checkout and breaks for every installed user. The
    drift check is what makes duplication safe.
  - ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} was chosen over ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} even though the
    corpus prefers the latter 40 references to 6. CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT resolves
    only when the whole plugin is installed; this repo also distributes through
    gh skill install, where it does not.
  - The executable-bit strip was found by measurement, not by reading: ship-check
    reported "executables shipped: NO" after the scripts were already in place,
    which is what prompted comparing source and installed permissions.

Deviations
  - ship-check's verdict changed shape. "Is anything executable" was the wrong
    question once the answer is always no; it now checks that each named script
    ships and is invoked through an interpreter, which is what actually breaks.
  - The proxy skill ships guile-repl-proxy.scm although its SKILL.md never
    invokes it. The skill documents the proxy, so a reader installing it alone
    can inspect the implementation the document describes.
